1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,132
One small edit to a help article.

2
00:00:02,182 --> 00:00:03,785
Thirty days becomes fourteen.

3
00:00:03,835 --> 00:00:06,180
Your support agent answers from this page.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,030
Golden Set shows, right on the page, which tested support answers this edit just made wrong.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:17,365
Golden Set.

6
00:00:17,415 --> 00:00:20,773
See which support answers break when you edit a help article.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,901
Golden Set keeps verified questions and answers from your resolved requests.

8
00:00:26,951 --> 00:00:29,340
Twelve of them rely on this article.

9
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:31,441
Eight now state the old window.

10
00:00:31,491 --> 00:00:35,101
For each one Golden Set suggests the corrected answer.

11
00:00:35,151 --> 00:00:40,658
This one it refuses to guess: the customer said the watch arrived three weeks ago.

12
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:43,573
With thirty days that customer was in time.

13
00:00:43,623 --> 00:00:45,470
With fourteen, they are not.

14
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:50,824
Swapping thirty for fourteen would read fine and be wrong, so a person decides.

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,080
Rewrite it, apply the rest, accept the edit.

16
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:58,232
Now the saved answers agree with the new article.

17
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:06,243
But was the prediction right?

18
00:01:06,293 --> 00:01:10,298
We ran Rovo Agent Evaluations on the same twelve questions.

19
00:01:10,348 --> 00:01:12,223
Before the edit: 92 percent.

20
00:01:12,273 --> 00:01:13,529
After the edit: 33.

21
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:20,058
The eight failures are exactly the eight answers Golden Set flagged, before any evaluation ran.

22
00:01:20,108 --> 00:01:22,464
After applying the suggestions: 83.

23
00:01:22,514 --> 00:01:28,100
The two misses are the three weeks case, and a question the article never covered.

24
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:34,300
The Golden Set agent answers in Rovo chat, and hands you the re-test file for Evaluations.

25
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:37,217
It never shows anything you could not open yourself.

26
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,916
Where do the golden answers come from?

27
00:01:43,966 --> 00:01:46,160
From your own resolved requests.

28
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,176
Golden Set keeps the ones that were solved:

29
00:01:49,226 --> 00:01:52,123
not reopened, no complaint, no low rating.

30
00:01:52,173 --> 00:01:56,401
It strips personal data and ties every answer to its article.

31
00:01:56,451 --> 00:01:57,734
Eighty requests in:

32
00:01:57,784 --> 00:02:02,644
fifteen rejected, five duplicates, ten in reserve, fifty golden pairs.

33
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:09,422
It compares the facts in each answer, numbers, money and durations, with the old and the new article.

34
00:02:09,472 --> 00:02:14,869
No language model of our own runs here, so it costs nothing and gives the same result every time.

35
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:18,744
It works without Rovo, and every view runs with your own permissions.

36
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,776
Evaluations give you a test runner.

37
00:02:21,826 --> 00:02:26,463
Golden Set gives you the test set, and tells you which tests each edit can break.

